Certificate authorities the client trusts, in addition to the Java runtime's own.

Every *.crt in this directory is built into the client jar and loaded by
ClientTrust at startup.  These are public certificates -- a CA's certificate is
the thing it hands out so that others can verify what it signs -- so there is
nothing secret about shipping them, and doing so means a downloaded client
trusts the private CA's servers with no per-machine setup.

lumpnet-ca.crt is ~/lump/config/keys/ca/pki/ca.crt: the Lumpnet Private
Certificate Authority root, which signs the certificates the front stack's
HAProxy presents.  When that CA is rotated, replace the file here and rebuild.
